['|Case|:**registration**\n```plaintext\nFUNCTION register()\n    IF METHOD IS POST THEN\n        username = request.form[\'username\']\n        password = request.form[\'password\']\n        email = request.form[\'email\']\n        \n        IF user_manager.register(username, password, email) THEN\n            RETURN redirect(url_for(\'login\'))\n        ENDIF\n    ENDIF\n    RENDER registration.html\nEND FUNCTION\n\nCLASS UserManager\n    FUNCTION register(username: str, password: str, email: str) -> bool\n        IF username already exists in users THEN\n            RETURN False\n        ENDIF\n        new_user = User(username, password, email)\n        APPEND new_user to users list\n        CALL save_users()\n        RETURN True\n    END FUNCTION\n\n    FUNCTION save_users()\n        OPEN \'users.txt\' FOR WRITING\n            FOR EACH user in users\n                WRITE user.username, user.password, user.email TO file\n            END FOR\n        CLOSE file\n    END FUNCTION\nEND CLASS\n\n<!-- registration.html -->\n<form method="POST" action="/register">\n    <label for="username">Username:</label>\n    <input type="text" id="username" name="username" required>\n    <label for="password">Password:</label>\n    <input type="password" id="password" name="password" required>\n    <label for="email">Email:</label>\n    <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required>\n    <button type="submit">Register</button>\n</form>\n```\n**Third-party Libraries Used**: \n- **Flask**: This web framework is used for routing and rendering templates. The `request`, `redirect`, and `url_for` features facilitate form handling and navigation.']
